  "en": "The pattern is the same for both, and it is the pattern that decided the top of this field: the judges score what the wiki shows. Reputation does not enter the ballot, and neither does work a judge cannot attribute or check. GreatBay-SCIE lost about three quarters of its gap to first place on pages that are empty rather than on experiments that failed. Lambert-GA lost most of its gap on one aspect, whether the project worked, because its one hard number came from a commercial vendor and its second arm produced none.\n\nThe same rule is why GEMS-Taiwan sits where it does. Our empty Attributions page costs us on the same aspect as GreatBay-SCIE's, and our Results banner claims a light switch our own figures do not show, which is the same kind of gap between claim and evidence that the judges penalised in Lambert-GA's home page.",
